=== The age of accountability
--- Romans 7:7-13: The Age of Accountability [title]
overline: Romans 7:7-13
sub: The Age of Accountability • The Holy Law Reveals Sin
refs: Romans 7:7-13

--- Key principle from Romans
callout: **Key Principle from Romans:** Where there is no law, sin is not imputed ([[Romans 4:15]]; [[Romans 5:13]]).
p: Without knowledge of God's commandment, there is no conscious transgression — and therefore no imputation of sin.

--- The Age of Accountability
p: Young children and the mentally challenged who lack the capacity to understand God's moral law are not condemned for sin in the same way as those who knowingly rebel.
p: God judges according to the light received — and where moral understanding is absent, He does not impute guilt.
p: After the death of the infant son born to David and Bathsheba, David declared with confidence:
scripture: 2 Samuel 12:23 | mark: I shall go to him, but he shall not return to me
p: —expressing his assurance that he would one day be reunited with his child in heaven.

--- Matthew 18:3
scripture: Matthew 18:3
p: Jesus holds up the humble, trusting nature of little children as the pattern for entering the kingdom — affirming their innocence and safe standing before God.

=== The wretched man: flesh vs. the inward man
--- Romans 7:13-25: Flesh vs. New Man [title]
overline: Romans 7:13-25
sub: The Sinful Flesh vs. The Inward Man • Despair & Triumph
refs: Romans 7:13-25

--- The inward man and the sinful flesh
table: The Inward Man (Renewed by the Spirit) | The Sinful Flesh (Indwelling Sin)
tr: Delights in the law of God (v.22) | Carnal, sold under sin (v.14)
tr: Consents that the law is good (v.16) | Dwells no good thing (v.18)
tr: Wills to do good (v.18, 21) | Does the evil I would not (v.19)
tr: Serves the law of God with the mind (v.25) | Serves the law of sin with the flesh (v.25)
tr: The real "I" of the believer | Another law warring & bringing into captivity (v.23)

--- Despair and triumph
scripture: Romans 7:24-25
p: "I myself" — the true believer, the inward man — is the real "I," the new creation that is the righteousness of God in Christ ([[2 Corinthians 5:21]]; [[Galatians 2:20]]).
p: The flesh is not our identity — it is crucified with Christ, dead and nailed to the cross ([[Romans 6:6]]; [[Colossians 2:14]]).
take: ([[Romans 7:25]]) — The door of hope that opens to the victory of chapter 8
